  "source_text": "Synthetic validation nurse note. No real patient data.\n\nThe driver has confirmed type 2 diabetes, and the current GP medication reconciliation states that diabetes is treated with oral medication. The driver takes the prescribed tablets and explicitly denies current insulin use; an old appointment reminder about discussing injectable options is not a prescription and has not been treated as evidence that an injection was started.\n\nAfter a delayed lunch last month he felt shaky and ate a snack without assistance, but glucose was measured only after the symptoms settled, so the nurse has no verified measurement during that event and no treating-clinician classification of severe hypoglycaemia. He has brought four weeks of glucose entries rather than a complete three-month record, and the specialist review has not yet occurred.\n\nHe also describes reduced radio clarity when the cab is noisy, although quiet conversation is easy and no complete audiogram accompanies the referral. His father used hearing aids, which does not establish the driver's threshold. The nurse records the confirmed diabetes and current oral treatment separately from the unclassified episode and the unmeasured hearing complaint.\n",
